# EnergyMind: Training AI Systems to Govern Scarce Resources Under Real-World Constraints

Most AI training environments optimize one clean objective.

Real systems do not.

In the real world, resources are limited, users have different priorities, feedback is delayed, and short-term decisions create long-term consequences. We built **EnergyMind** to train AI systems in exactly that kind of setting.

EnergyMind is an OpenEnv-compatible, human-aware multi-agent governance environment where an agent allocates scarce electricity across a shared hostel. The task is not just to save energy. The task is to make tradeoffs between comfort, fairness, high-priority needs, complaint control, and hard power-budget limits.

That shift matters. It turns the problem from simple optimization into governance under scarcity.

