## Final System Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["Environment State<br/>occupancy, priority, complaints, budget, heatwave"] --> B["Observation Builder"]
    B --> C["LLM Planner"]
    C --> D["High-Level Strategy<br/>priority_safe, complaint_rescue, energy_saver, ..."]
    D --> E["Low-Level Executor<br/>Q-learning / Centralized DQN"]
    E --> F["Safe Execution Layer"]
    F --> G["Room-Level Actions<br/>10 actions, one per room"]
    G --> H["EnergyMind Environment Step"]
    H --> I["Reward + Score + Diagnostics"]
    I --> J["Training Signals"]
    J --> K["RL Update"]
    J --> L["LLM Post-Training Update"]
This hybrid architecture is the core systems contribution of EnergyMind.

The LLM handles reasoning at the right level of abstraction. The executor handles repeated constrained control. The environment provides accountability.

How the LLM Actually Works
The LLM does not output arbitrary appliance commands.

Instead, it sees a structured summary of the current hostel state and chooses one strategy from a bounded strategy set such as:

priority_safe
complaint_rescue
energy_saver
comfort_all
shutdown_empty
do_nothing
That strategy is then translated into valid room-level actions by the executor.

